    "result": "I found no defects in this diff.\n\nIt's a behavior-preserving refactor. I checked each path against the old code:\n\n- **`Approve`:** The old code set `Status`, `DecidedBy` and `DecidedAt`, called `_repository.Update`, and returned the invoice. `Decide` does the same with `Approved`.\n- **`Reject`:** The only change is that `DecisionNote` is now set before `Status`, `DecidedBy` and `DecidedAt` instead of after. Nothing reads those fields in between, and `Update` still runs after all of them. If `Update` threw, the invoice would already be partly mutated in memory, but that was also true before.\n- **Guards:** `Find`, `EnsurePending` and the argument validation sit above the changed lines, so they run in the same order as before.\n- **`Decide`:** It's private and has two callers. It adds no new public surface or null handling.\n\nI could only see this hunk, not the whole file. If `Approve` or `Reject` set other fields elsewhere, or `Decide` is meant to be shared with other callers, I couldn't check that. Confidence that the visible change is correct is high.",
